    "created_at": "2026-11-21T22:27:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-21T22:27:19Z",
    "body": "Cause found: not the code. Both red runs (`6ffa808ae` #2714 `ui suites: trace_parity`, `273642212` #3185 `ui suites: lib`) ran on two of the post-merge runners added today. Each failed in 1-2 s with `exit -1`. The kernel log on those machines shows a segfault inside `libvulkan.so` at those exact times: the UI tests' Vulkan loader picked the machine's real GPU driver, which the unprivileged runner account cannot use, and crashed.\n\nFix (runner environment only, no code change): every post-merge runner's `.env` now pins Mesa's software renderer, the same one the GPU-less runners already use: `VK_ICD_FILENAMES` / `VK_DRIVER_FILES` = `/usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/lvp_icd.json`, `LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1`. Each runner restarts with it when it is idle. A re-run of `trace_parity` on `2d98d87be` passes (comment above), so the next green run should close this issue.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
